## Objective

Complete the still-required Platform production-activation child without replacing the child or resetting correction history. The immediate objective is to close the repository-side secret-surface/provenance acceptance chain, then proceed through the separately gated live production sequence owned by #164.

## Scope

#164 durably owns:

- PR #173 repository/candidate acceptance;
- secret-surface/runtime-connection correctness;
- production DB preparation after repository finality;
- at-most-once migration `0010` under separate authority;
- runtime DB binding;
- Auth0-only production authentication configuration;
- Coolify production application preparation;
- real Platform↔SQAG Auth0/launch linkage;
- final return for first production deployment/go-live after the programme hard pre-go-live dependency block is satisfied.

The child is not replaced by G4 AMEND, correction exhaustion, G1/G2 re-entry, worker replacement, validation-environment HOLD or Web-directed continuation exhaustion.

## Current accepted architecture / executable contract

The existing Run-691 external-database capability-auth architecture remains unchanged. Run-694 G2 additionally reclosed the parent public-return contract.

Current public-return contract:

- successful public completion requires static proof, migration success, authority/receipt revocation, required Pool cleanup, closed invocation, validated privileged-child exit/result, source release, parent callback exactly once after those events, successful callback settlement, and admissible public data;
- clean public data includes proven-clean primitive/string/null/undefined, plain objects, arrays, clean cyclic graphs, and verified intrinsic Map/Set;
- forbidden public data includes custom class instances as public objects, callables, custom thenables, iterators/generators, accessor-bearing objects, custom observation/coercion hooks, opaque WeakMap/WeakSet-like containers, and credential/diagnostic/authority/capability/private-state-bearing values;
- unknown provenance/proxy/prototype/slot/traversal/scheduling state fails closed;
- direct return, `await 0`, and verified native-Promise scheduling are semantically equivalent when receiver/effects/lifecycle are proven equivalent;
- clean cycles are allowed with cycle-aware identity tracking and must not hide secret/prototype/symbol/private-state surfaces;
- RAW clean returns that skip the required callback are `AP_OPERATION` RED, not automatically public-escape RED;
- callbac
